  A.tf("b2-q25", "Easy", "UCS is complete and cost-optimal when all step costs are positive.", true, "UCS expands in order of g, so the first goal popped is cheapest.", "UCS: complete + optimal (costs ≥ ε > 0).", P(25, s, { trap: false }));
  A.tf("b2-q26", "Medium", "Greedy best-first search is cost-optimal if the heuristic is admissible.", false, "Greedy ignores g. Admissibility makes A* optimal, not greedy (Romania: 450 vs 418).", "Admissible h helps A*, not greedy.", P(26, g));
